WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:08.254
The United Nations Committee on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities declared Canada's MAID program a matter of extreme concern in March 2025.

00:00:08.204 --> 00:00:14.863
Seventy-six thousand, seven hundred and seven disabled and vulnerable people killed through MAID since 2016.

00:00:14.863 --> 00:00:20.636
Canada ratified the UN Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities in 2014.

00:00:20.636 --> 00:00:25.272
Then built a death program that violates eleven articles of that same convention.

00:00:25.272 --> 00:00:32.613
Track 2 expansion — MAID for mental illness as a sole condition — was approved despite UN objections and provincial opposition.

00:00:32.613 --> 00:00:36.409
The UN Committee demanded the immediate repeal of Track 2.

00:00:36.409 --> 00:00:39.954
The government's response: no implementation plan.

00:00:39.954 --> 00:00:41.999
Canada signed the treaty.

00:00:41.999 --> 00:00:43.988
Canada broke the treaty.

00:00:43.988 --> 00:00:46.636
The international community noticed.

00:00:46.636 --> 00:00:48.670
Canada does not care.
